159|n|Something joined or added to another thing, but not essentially a part of it. ; A person joined to another in some duty or service; a colleague; an associate. ; A word or words added to quality or amplify the force of other words; as, the History of the American Revolution, where the words in italics are the adjunct or adjuncts of "History." ; A quality or property of the body or the mind, whether natural or acquired; as, color, in the body, judgment in the mind. ; A key or scale closely related to another as principal; a relative or attendant key. [R.] See Attendant keys, under Attendant, a.	V:22pd,33,1;29x0,9,1~22pd,33,1;29x0,9,1	N:rgi,63,7~rgi,63,7
