16n|a|Pertaining to administration; administering; executive; as, an administrative body, ability, or energy.	j:n67,91,7;22lc,78,9;19k8,72,2;1n1f,67,4;1lqx,67,10;1yz9,67,5;555,65,4;4zy,60,3;w95,51,8;14p8,38,4;14bn,38,4;1n1c,35,3;2b4n,24,7~1lqx,67,10;22lc,78,9;w95,51,8;2b4n,24,7;n67,91,7;1yz9,67,5;14bn,38,4;14p8,38,4;1n1f,67,4;555,65,4;4zy,60,3;1n1c,35,3;19k8,72,2
16o|n|One who administers affairs; one who directs, manages, executes, or dispenses, whether in civil, judicial, political, or ecclesiastical affairs; a manager. ; A man who manages or settles the estate of an intestate, or of a testator when there is no competent executor; one to whom the right of administration has been committed by competent authority.	n:1r8m,46,5~1r8m,46,5
